  "factCheck": {
    "status": "verified",
    "by": "HeyMariner daily desk",
    "checkedAt": "2026-11-14",
    "notes": "Checked against MSC.576(110): climb 1.5-9 m and combination above 9 m (3.2); clear of discharges, parallel body, steps firmly against ship's side, lowest step as pilot requests (12); strong points/shackles breaking strength not less than 48 kN (6.1); never secured to accommodation ladder lower platform (13.1.6); lifebuoy with self-igniting light, heaving line, two manropes (15.1); responsible officer with communication to bridge (3.7); inspection before and after each use (25.1); withdrawal at 30 months in service or 36 months from manufacture (30). 1 January 2028 application of stowage/maintenance/inspection/operation parts confirmed by DNV (amended SOLAS V/23, MSC.572(110))."
  },
  "meta": {
    "description": "How to rig a pilot ladder the way the new IMO pilot transfer standards require: 1.5 to 9 metres climb, position clear of discharges and flat on the hull, 48 kN strong points and the gear at the access point. From 1 January 2028 ladders also leave service after 30 months in use or 36 months from manufacture.",
